  <language>fr_FR</language>
  <keyword>isnat</keyword>
  <short_description>Teste les elements datetime not-a-time.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>tf = isnat(t)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>inputs</param_name>
      <param_description>Un tableau datetime.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output</param_name>
      <param_description>Un tableau logique avec true lorsque les dates serie datetime sont NaN.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Teste les elements datetime not-a-time.</p>
    <p>isnat rejette les entrees non datetime. C est le test de valeur manquante propre a datetime et il conserve la forme des donnees datetime.</p>
    <p>Array-valued inputs keep their data shape when the operation supports arrays. Scalar operands are expanded where the implementation defines scalar expansion.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description>Utilisation de base.</example_item_description>
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[t = [datetime(2024,1,1), NaT]
isnat(t)
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
